# Copy to ~/.dori/dori.env (a second Dori: its own directory, e.g. ~/.second/dori.env) and chmod 600. Every dori command and
# every unit in systemd/ reads it. It holds this Dori's secrets and ids: it stays local and is never committed.
# What each variable turns on: README.md, "Settings per Dori". A feature whose variables are unset is off.
# The ids below are placeholders: turn on Developer Mode in Discord, then right-click > Copy ID.

# Bot token (Developer Portal > your app > Bot > Reset Token). Turn on the Message Content intent there too.
DORI_DISCORD_TOKEN=replace-with-your-bot-token
# The server, the one channel the Dori talks in, and the owner's user id.
DORI_DISCORD_GUILD=111111111111111111
DORI_DISCORD_CHANNEL=222222222222222222
DORI_DISCORD_OWNER=333333333333333333

# The Dori's own aoe session: id from `aoe list --json`, tmux name from `tmux ls`.
DORI_LEAD_AOE_ID=0a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b
DORI_LEAD_TMUX=aoe_Dori_0a1b2c3d
# Optional. The agent CLI self-restart.sh waits for in the lead's pane (default omo).
# DORI_AGENT_BIN=omo

# Optional. Id of the owner's own webhook in that channel (e.g. an iOS Shortcut voice upload); its posts count as the
# owner's. Leave unset until the first post logs DISCORD_WEBHOOK_UNKNOWN id=... See ios-shortcut-voice.md.
# DORI_DISCORD_OWNER_WEBHOOK=
# Optional. Inbox file the listener appends to (default ~/.dori/state/discord/inbox.jsonl).
# DORI_DISCORD_INBOX=
# Optional. Where question cards and answers live (default ~/.dori/state/discord).
# DORI_DISCORD_STATE_DIR=
# Optional. A channel shared with a second Dori and that Dori's bot id: rows with scope "pair" / "pair-bot".
# DORI_DISCORD_PAIR_CHANNEL=
# DORI_DISCORD_PAIR_BOT=
# Shadow run only, never in this file: DORI_DISCORD_SHADOW_INBOX=<file> (see README, "Switching an existing listener over").
# Optional. Speech-to-text install dir and language for transcribe.sh (default ~/.dori/asr, auto).
# DORI_ASR_DIR=
# DORI_ASR_LANG=en
# Optional. whisper.cpp model file for setup-asr.sh and transcribe.sh (default ggml-large-v3.bin).
# DORI_ASR_MODEL=ggml-large-v3.bin

# Optional Google watcher (read-only zele). All paths must be absolute.
# DORI_GOOGLE_ACCOUNT=account@example.com
# DORI_GOOGLE_EVENTS=/absolute/path/google-events.jsonl
# DORI_GOOGLE_STATE=/absolute/path/google-watch.state.json
# DORI_GOOGLE_INTERVAL_MS=120000
# DORI_GOOGLE_WINDOW_MIN=35
# DORI_GOOGLE_TIME_ZONE=UTC
# Full host PATH including zele and its Node runtime (e.g. nvm); overrides the unit default.
# PATH=/absolute/path/node/bin:/absolute/path/bun/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# Optional KakaoTalk watcher (kakao-watch.ts), only for a Dori with its own Kakao account; off while SELF_ID is unset.
# DORI_KAKAO_SELF_ID=111111111
# DORI_KAKAO_OWNER_ID=222222222
# Quoted: self-restart.sh sources this file with the shell, where a bare | starts a pipeline.
# DORI_KAKAO_MENTION='dori|도리'
# DORI_KAKAO_STATE_DIR=/absolute/path/state
# DORI_KAKAO_INBOX=/absolute/path/state/discord/inbox.jsonl
# DORI_KAKAO_CLI=agent-messenger
# DORI_KAKAO_POLL_MS=8000
# DORI_KAKAO_SWEEP_MS=300000
# DORI_KAKAO_DISCOVER_MS=20000
# Login only (kakao-login.ts). The account file holds KAKAO_EMAIL / KAKAO_PASSWORD: a separate 0600 file, not this one.
# DORI_KAKAO_ACCOUNT_FILE=/absolute/path/kakao.env
# DORI_KAKAO_DEVICE_TYPE=tablet

# Usage screenshot: omo-usage checkout is required; Firefox snap working directory is optional.
# DORI_USAGE_DIR=/absolute/path/omo-usage
# DORI_USAGE_SNAP_DIR=/absolute/path/firefox-accessible-directory

# Optional other messengers (dori send slack|telegram, dori presence, dori inbound slack). Secrets.
# DORI_SLACK_TOKEN=replace-with-slack-token
# DORI_SLACK_COOKIE=replace-with-slack-d-cookie
# DORI_TELEGRAM_TOKEN=123456789:replace-with-telegram-bot-token
